ar/lib/secure-volume/secure.img, mapper name secure_srv) on node1, formatted it XFS, and mounted it at /srv/secure. Configured /etc/crypttab and /etc/fstab with a root-fs-resident keyfile (/etc/luks-keys/secure.key, mode 400) so it unlocks and mounts automatically at boot with no manual intervention. Verified end-to-end with a full node reboot: boot_id changed (fbdf5b2c... -> 175dd2d7...), the cryptsetup and mount systemd units came up active on their own, and pre-restart test data written to /srv/secure survived.\",\"actions_performed\":[\"Inspected node1 disks/OS: RHEL 9.8, single 20G root disk, no spare block device available\",\"Installed cryptsetup package via dnf\",\"Created 2GiB backing file /var/lib/secure-volume/secure.img and a random keyfile /etc/luks-keys/secure.key (mode 400)\",\"Ran cryptsetup luksFormat on the backing file using the keyfile\",\"Opened the LUKS volume as secure_srv, created an XFS filesystem, created /srv/secure mount point\",\"Added crypttab entry (secure_srv, backing file path, keyfile, luks) and fstab entry (UUID of mapped fs, /srv/secure, xfs)\",\"Verified mount -a mounts cleanly, fixed SELinux labeling with restorecon\",\"Inspected generated systemd units (systemd-cryptsetup@secure_srv.service, srv-secure.mount) confirming correct RequiresMountsFor/ordering dependencies for boot-time auto-unlock\",\"Captured pre-restart baseline: boot_id, mount state, and wrote baseline.txt test data into /srv/secure\",\"Issued systemctl reboot on node1; acknowledgement returned before the connection dropped\",\"Polled node1 until exec access returned; confirmed new boot_id and uptime 0 (fresh boot)\",\"Verified post-restart state: /srv/secure auto-mounted, cryptsetup and mount systemd units active, baseline.txt data intact\"],\"evidence\":[{\"requirement\":\"Encrypted (LUKS2) volume created, formatted, and mounted at /srv/secure\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-e9851cf905784163\",\"cmd-535ef813cf0d49a3\",\"cmd-8c13c9c2aa6f4c78\"],\"summary\":\"Backing file created, cryptsetup luksFormat succeeded producing a LUKS UUID, mapped device formatted XFS\"},{\"requirement\":\"Volume unlocks and mounts automatically without manual steps (config in place)\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-dbb0182889c0422c\",\"cmd-e4ddcd5a762148c6\",\"cmd-c858b107ca2743c8\",\"cmd-278b2a2a571c4273\"],\"summary\":\"crypttab/fstab entries added, mount -a succeeded and SELinux relabeled, generated systemd-cryptsetup@secure_srv.service and srv-secure.mount units show correct dependency ordering for boot-time activation\"},{\"requirement\":\"Healthy baseline captured before restart (boot identity + service/data health)\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-cb190f7c3fd140a2\"],\"summary\":\"Captured pre-restart boot_id (fbdf5b2c-bb43-49f6-935d-fb98f8a972f6), confirmed /srv/secure mounted, wrote baseline-data test file\"},{\"requirement\":\"Node restart acknowledged and executed one at a time via native safe mechanism\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-497e459940f74a69\"],\"summary\":\"systemctl reboot issued in background; command returned/disconnected before restart completed, confirming acknowledgement was returned pre-disconnect\"},{\"requirement\":\"Node became reachable again with proof of changed boot identity\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-465f7fe2eca54309\"],\"summary\":\"exec succeeded again showing new boot_id 175dd2d7-9999-4453-86de-3b5a9a28db98 (different from baseline) and uptime 0 minutes, proving an actual reboot occurred\"},{\"requirement\":\"Post-restart recovery of required service, mount, and data verified\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-7670477a76854ec6\"],\"summary\":\"After reboot, /srv/secure is mounted via /dev/mapper/secure_srv, systemd-cryptsetup@secure_srv.service and srv-secure.mount are active, cryptsetup status shows the LUKS2 mapping active, and baseline.txt content 'baseline-data' was read back intact\"}]}","structured_output":{"status":"completed","summary":"Created a LUKS2-encrypted volume (2GiB file-backed loop device at /var/lib/secure-volume/secure.img, mapper name secure_srv) on node1, formatted it XFS, and mounted it at /srv/secure. Configured /etc/crypttab and /etc/fstab with a root-fs-resident keyfile (/etc/luks-keys/secure.key, mode 400) so it unlocks and mounts automatically at boot with no manual intervention. Verified end-to-end with a full node reboot: boot_id changed (fbdf5b2c... -> 175dd2d7...), the cryptsetup and mount systemd units came up active on their own, and pre-restart test data written to /srv/secure survived.","actions_performed":["Inspected node1 disks/OS: RHEL 9.8, single 20G root disk, no spare block device available","Installed cryptsetup package via dnf","Created 2GiB backing file /var/lib/secure-volume/secure.img and a random keyfile /etc/luks-keys/secure.key (mode 400)","Ran cryptsetup luksFormat on the backing file using the keyfile","Opened the LUKS volume as secure_srv, created an XFS filesystem, created /srv/secure mount point","Added crypttab entry (secure_srv, backing file path, keyfile, luks) and fstab entry (UUID of mapped fs, /srv/secure, xfs)","Verified mount -a mounts cleanly, fixed SELinux labeling with restorecon","Inspected generated systemd units (systemd-cryptsetup@secure_srv.service, srv-secure.mount) confirming correct RequiresMountsFor/ordering dependencies for boot-time auto-unlock","Captured pre-restart baseline: boot_id, mount state, and wrote baseline.txt test data into /srv/secure","Issued systemctl reboot on node1; acknowledgement returned before the connection dropped","Polled node1 until exec access returned; confirmed new boot_id and uptime 0 (fresh boot)","Verified post-restart state: /srv/secure auto-mounted, cryptsetup and mount systemd units active, baseline.txt data intact"],"evidence":[{"requirement":"Encrypted (LUKS2) volume created, formatted, and mounted at /srv/secure","command_ids":["cmd-e9851cf905784163","cmd-535ef813cf0d49a3","cmd-8c13c9c2aa6f4c78"],"summary":"Backing file created, cryptsetup luksFormat succeeded producing a LUKS UUID, mapped device formatted XFS"},{"requirement":"Volume unlocks and mounts automatically without manual steps (config in place)","command_ids":["cmd-dbb0182889c0422c","cmd-e4ddcd5a762148c6","cmd-c858b107ca2743c8","cmd-278b2a2a571c4273"],"summary":"crypttab/fstab entries added, mount -a succeeded and SELinux relabeled, generated systemd-cryptsetup@secure_srv.service and srv-secure.mount units show correct dependency ordering for boot-time activation"},{"requirement":"Healthy baseline captured before restart (boot identity + service/data health)","command_ids":["cmd-cb190f7c3fd140a2"],"summary":"Captured pre-restart boot_id (fbdf5b2c-bb43-49f6-935d-fb98f8a972f6), confirmed /srv/secure mounted, wrote baseline-data test file"},{"requirement":"Node restart acknowledged and executed one at a time via native safe mechanism","command_ids":["cmd-497e459940f74a69"],"summary":"systemctl reboot issued in background; command returned/disconnected before restart completed, confirming acknowledgement was returned pre-disconnect"},{"requirement":"Node became reachable again with proof of changed boot identity","command_ids":["cmd-465f7fe2eca54309"],"summary":"exec succeeded again showing new boot_id 175dd2d7-9999-4453-86de-3b5a9a28db98 (different from baseline) and uptime 0 minutes, proving an actual reboot occurred"},{"requirement":"Post-restart recovery of required service, mount, and data verified","command_ids":["cmd-7670477a76854ec6"],"summary":"After reboot, /srv/secure is mounted via /dev/mapper/secure_srv, systemd-cryptsetup@secure_srv.service and srv-secure.mount are active, cryptsetup status shows the LUKS2 mapping active, and baseline.txt content 'baseline-data' was read back intact"}]},"ttft_ms":5237,"type":"result","duration_ms":141734,"uuid":"054adf46-dba9-4c6c-a5b4-42a2948082e4","ttft_stream_ms":3547,"time_to_request_ms":43,"first_content_frame_ms":4041,"queued_turn_count":0}
